  "content": "Gold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nOnlinekhabar\nTuesday, October 7, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 7\nA surge in international gold prices has driven the domestic bullion market to an all-time high.\nAccording to the Federation of Gold and Silver Dealers’ Association, gold was traded at Rs 235,960 per tola (11.66 grams) today, up from Rs 233,100 per tola on Monday.\nSimilarly, silver is priced at Rs 2,930 per tola. In the international market, gold is being traded at 3,965 US dollars per ounce.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nElection Commission\nlichhibari land scam\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\n3 days ago\nGold price reaches record high\n2 weeks ago\nGold price hikes by Rs 1,100 per tola\n3 weeks ago\nGold prices hit new record, rise by Rs 1,600 per tola\n1 month ago\nGold price hits record high at Rs 205,900 per tola\n1 month ago\nGold price hits record high, crosses Rs 200,000 per tola\n1 month ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nMonsoon triggers flood and landslide risks in several districts, DHM issues special alert\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nCAA publishes domestic airfare rates, Kathmandu–Dhangadhi at Rs 17,579\nLiving Goddess Kumari to offer Dashain Tika to public today\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nPolitics\nElection Commission invites parties for talks on upcoming House election\n12 hours ago\nSociety\nSeven charged in Pokhara Lichhibari land scam involving former ministers and officials\n12 hours ago\nOpinion\nWhen a joke fuels division: Casual hate speech and the Gen Z revolution in Nepal\n19 hours ago\nBlog\nWhen Nepal’s youth dared to dream of a better tomorrow\n2 days ago\nSociety\nAI and fake accounts drove one third of online buzz during Nepal Gen Z uprising\n2 days ago",
